From 6d0ed15c06a8906c8908910447e63adc948129f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:53:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 127/128] gxcore: a draw's vertex constants kept when its
 transform state is the draw before's

Every draw rebuilt its 2.8 KB vertex constant block from the transform state
the front end snapshotted for it (the whole plan, constants included, was
cleared first), and the submission layer then compared all 2.8 KB with the
block it pushed last - though most draws repeat the draw before's (96
percent in the Forsaken Fortress). On four of the i9's E-cores a profile of
the GX worker put its copying (clearing, building, comparing, keeping
copies) at about 30 percent of its working time, the compare alone the
largest part.

The transform state now has a version (dol_gx_recomp_xf_version): one
counter, changed by every XF load that reaches what a draw snapshots, by
matrix index A, an init, post-transform memory and a loaded state. It is
kept outside DolGxRecompState, so saved states keep their size and load as
before. The snapshot, the draw packet and the consumed draw carry it. A plan
keeps its constants through the next draw's reset (DrawPlanFields is
everything else); the builder makes them anew only when the version or the
shader key bits they depend on (lighting, the lit channels, the texgens and
their projection, the incoming cached normal) differ from what they were made
from, and gives each block it makes a new constants_id. The submission layer
takes a plan whose id is the block it pushed last as repeating it, without
comparing, and compares the others as before (they may still be the same
bytes). The per-texgen matrix rows and the unresolved-matrix count are kept
with the constants. DOL_GXCORE_CONSTANTS_VERIFY=1 makes kept constants again
and compares them; DOL_GXCORE_CONSTANTS_KEEP=0 always makes them.

Checked on the i9 + RTX 5090 (BlueWake):
- Kept constants against remade ones, bit for bit, everywhere reachable:
  the Outset route (12.7 million draws), three save states (Gohma's room,
  Dragon Roost Cavern's lava room and bridge) and five warps (the Flight
  Control Platform, sea rooms 25 and 11, Dragon Roost Cavern, Forest
  Haven): no difference.
- Smooth Motion dumps, game frames 880-910, identical to the build before
  (62 of 62); gxcore_tests and frame_interp_test pass.
- Four E-cores, unpaced, Smooth Motion off (a fixed amount of work), kept
  against always made, four runs each, interleaved: the GX worker's CPU per
  game frame 16.4-17.0 ms against 18.8-19.2 (12 percent less), and the game,
  which waits on the GX worker at its draw-done barriers, at 34.0-34.7 game
  frames a second against 32.9-33.5; the game thread's own CPU per frame the
  same (23.5-24.5 ms). Paced at Smooth Motion 60 both held full speed.
